Build **Hollowdeep**, a side-view sealed-colony survival simulation that runs
entirely in the browser — and **produce its art, effects, and audio yourself**,
during this build, with the asset-generation tools on your `PATH`.

Your project root is `{{workspace}}`. Create the game there.

## Your starting point

A starter project is already in place at `{{workspace}}`: a `package.json` that
pins **Playwright** as a dev dependency and depends on the
**`@test-cabinet/particle-runtime`** library (below). Its dependencies have already
been installed for you — `node_modules/` is populated and Playwright's headless
**Chromium** is downloaded — so you can build and verify right away. Build on this
project rather than replacing it: keep the `package.json`, add your framework,
bundler, and a `build` script on top of it, and keep the lockfile in sync (see
below).

## What to read first

The full specification is split across the files below, all already present in
your project. Read every one of them before you start, then implement the game
they describe as a single, cohesive build:

{{#each specs}}
- `{{this.path}}`
